      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "During the past five years percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) and intracoronary infusion of streptokinase have been introduced and rapidly accepted as new methods for the treatment of patients with ischemic heart disease. Both of these methods hold great promise for the future. PTCA is established as useful in some selected patients while intracoronary streptokinase is still investigational."},
